From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: let VA capture use four channels

The back-end fixup forces every back end to two channels (the TX codec
DMA interfaces may also go down to one), so a four-channel capture on
VA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0 reaches the codec DMA as two channels, whatever the
front end and the topology allow.

The VA macro has four decimators. When the front end asks for four
channels, keep four at the back end, one decimator per channel. Other
boards on this machine driver whose topology lets VA capture use four
channels, such as the QCM6490 IDP, get four as well; requests for one
or two channels stay as they were.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@
 	struct snd_interval *channels = hw_param_interval(params,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS);
 	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);
+	unsigned int fe_channels = params_channels(params);
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
@@ -102,6 +103,11 @@
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
 		channels->min = 1;
 		break;
+	case VA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
+		/* Up to four decimators, one per channel, if the FE asks. */
+		if (fe_channels == 4)
+			channels->min = channels->max = 4;
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
